  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The pressure versus temperature graph of an ideal gas is shown in the figure below. If the density of gas at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#961;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>, then the density of the gas at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;will be</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/a38ea51e-bfc8-4676-a99c-366ff646d4c0-image.png\" style=\"width: 313px; height: 238px;\" /></p>",
